        "original_id": "4e679d82-cc58-5d24-8651-f2e5b9696192",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Valie Export, Gary Sherman\n- Works: The Practice of Love, Death Line, Dead & Buried, Poltergeist III\n- Roles: film director, screenwriter, producer, artist\n- Topics: horror film genre, contemporary arts\n\nFacts:\n- Gary Sherman was born in 1945 and is an American film director, screenwriter, and producer from Chicago, Illinois.\n- Valie Export's artistic work includes video installations, body performances, expanded cinema, computer animations, photography, sculptures, and publications covering contemporary arts.\n- In 1985, The Practice of Love (German: Die Praxis der Liebe) was released as an Austrian drama film written and directed by Valie Export.\n- Gary Sherman is best known for prolific work in the horror film genre, including directing Death Line, Dead & Buried, and Poltergeist III.",
